// macro-parenthesis-adjacency.  Measured against the established compiler.
// A lone '(' as an OBJECT-like body (note the space).  The established compiler takes it
// as the body and fails in the parser - C0000 "syntax error, unexpected ';'"
// - NOT as a bad definition.  Pinned so the C0105 check above cannot creep
// onto the object-like side.
#define K (
float4 main(float4 t : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR { return t * K; }
